cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these tables, please cite them and the work of Antieau, Krause and Nikolaus on
  which the computation rests.
title: "FiniteChainSyntomicCohomology: p-adic K-groups of finite chain rings in degrees up to 100"
abstract: >-
  The p-adic K-groups K_r(R; Z_p), 1 <= r <= 100, of finite chain rings R = O_K/pi^n, computed
  with Syntomic.jl: the 19 rings Z/p^n tabulated in Appendix A of Antieau, Krause and Nikolaus,
  On the K-theory of Z/p^n, and the 64 rings O_K/pi^n, 2 <= n <= 5, of the 16 quadratic
  extensions K of Q_2, Q_3, Q_5 and Q_7. The groups that are new relative to that appendix are
  marked.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Ong
    given-names: Wern Juin Gabriel
    email: gabriel_ong@ieee.org
repository-code: "https://github.com/wgabrielong/FiniteChainSyntomicCohomology"
keywords:
  - algebraic K-theory
  - syntomic cohomology
  - finite chain rings
  - p-adic fields
references:
